<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">War Jabi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 1040</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as War Jaabi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">War Jabi was a ruler of Takrur in the middle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/senegal">Senegal</a> valley and one of the first West African kings to adopt <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a>, according to the geographer al-Bakri. He imposed Islamic law on his subjects, and his son Labi fought alongside the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almoravid-empire">Almoravids</a> against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gudala">Gudala</a> in 1056.</p></div>
